  "description_html": "Size comparison of the Triassic theropod dinosaur <i>Coelophysis bauri</i>. The depicted specimen is AMNH 7223, the largest exemplar of this species known from good remains, which has an axial length of 2.62 m (8.6 ft). The silhouette was drawn after Hartman's skeletal, then modified following the measurements and photographs given by Colbert (1989). The human silhouette 180 cm is from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silhouette_of_man_standing_and_facing_forward.svg\" title=\"File:Silhouette of man standing and facing forward.svg\">File:Silhouette of man standing and facing forward.svg</a> (CC0).\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Colbert, E. (1989). \"The Triassic dinosaur <i>Coelophysis</i>\". <i>Museum of Northern Arizona Bulletin</i> <b>57</b>: 1–160.</cite></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.skeletaldrawing.com/theropods/coelophysis\">Skeletal diagram by Scott Hartman</a></li></ul>",
